# dotfiles (chezmoi-managed macOS)

Work-machine dotfiles for `github.com/nrs-cpawela/dotfiles` (macOS now; Windows apply later). Edit source under `home/`, never live `~/.foo` files.

New session or cloud agent: read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) first; invoke `/resume-dotfiles` to reconstruct git state and continue without redoing landed work.

## Architecture

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `home/` | Chezmoi source (`dot_foo` → `~/.foo`, `private_dot_ssh/` → `~/.ssh/`, `private_` files mode 600, `.tmpl` for templates) |
| `Brewfile` | Core dotfiles-required CLI tools only |
| `Brewfile.cli` | Daily CLI toolkit (cloud, k8s, langs, etc.) |
| `Brewfile.apps` | GUI apps (Rectangle, Slack, Spotify, …) |
| `Brewfile.archive` | Gitignored historical reference — do not resurrect or commit |
| `Extfile` | Editor extensions installed into both VS Code and Cursor |
| `Extfile.vscode` / `Extfile.cursor` | Editor-locked extensions (marketplace split) |
| `Extfile.ignore` | Installed locally but unreproducible — never installed, silenced in diff |
| `Makefile` | Single entry point — `make help` lists all targets |
| `scripts/` | Helpers invoked by the Makefile (e.g. `ext.sh`) |
| `.pre-commit-config.yaml` + `.gitleaks.toml` | Secret scanning (keep) |
| `Skillfile` / `Skillfile.lock` / `vendor/` | Personal Cursor skills and their upstreams; `vendor/` is pristine upstream, never edit it |

## Conventions

- **Git identity:** path-based via `includeIf` in `dot_gitconfig.tmpl` — `~/development/*` → work, `~/home/*` and `~/dotfiles` → personal. Independent of OS. Do not collapse to a single identity.
- **Chezmoi:** no home/work prompt. `sourceDir` is `~/dotfiles`. Windows is a separate apply path.
- **Editor extensions:** the `Extfile` set is the source of truth. VS Code Settings Sync only reaches other VS Code installs (Microsoft restricts it to official builds), and VS Code uses the Microsoft Marketplace while Cursor uses OpenVSX — so parity is a shared baseline plus a deliberate per-editor delta, never one list.

## Workflows

- Track new dotfile: `chezmoi add ~/.foo` or edit `home/` + `make apply`
- Add dotfile-required CLI: edit `Brewfile` + `make brew-bundle`
- Add daily CLI tool: edit `Brewfile.cli` + `make cli`
- Add GUI app: edit `Brewfile.apps` + `make apps`
- Add editor extension: install it in either editor, then `make ext-dump` + `make ext` (or edit `Extfile` directly + `make ext`)
- Remove editor extension: delete the line from the `Extfile` set, then `make ext-prune` (dry-run) and `make ext-prune FORCE=1` — uninstalling in the GUI alone gets undone by the next `make ext`
- Check editor drift: `make ext-diff`
- Apply changes: `make apply`
- Full sync: `make sync`
- Check for leaks: `make lint`
- Check skills against upstream: `make skills`
- Take upstream skill changes: `make skills-pull NAME=x`, review `git diff`, then `make apply`

## Do NOT

- Put SOPS/age/Bitwarden into chezmoi apply or core `Brewfile` — repo files stay plaintext; those CLIs may live in `Brewfile.cli` as optional tools only
- Commit `Brewfile.archive` (gitignored)
- Add work hostnames, IPs, employer names, or fleet details to committed files (public repo). Work-derived skills go in the private work repo, not `Skillfile`
- Run `npx skills update` on Skillfile skills — it overwrites local edits
- Edit `~/.zshrc`, `~/.gitconfig`, or other live home files — edit `home/` source + `make apply`
- Add daily CLI tools or GUI apps to `Brewfile` — use `Brewfile.cli` or `Brewfile.apps` instead
- Put an extension in `Extfile` unless it resolves on **both** the Microsoft Marketplace and OpenVSX — otherwise `make ext` fails on the editor that can't reach it

## Before commit

```bash
make lint    # gitleaks, detect-secrets, yaml, EOF, whitespace
make apply   # verify chezmoi templates parse
```

